    "turn_text": "The party is scheduled to vote, and I think that what's going on right now is that if I think people are going home letting tempers decompress a little bit, coming back together, starting on Tuesday, going to do a candidate for them and have people that are interested in the speaker's role talking about their candidacy and what they want to do, and then ideally a vote on Wednesday. But I want to remind you, Jake, going back to January, Even without all the sore wounds then, it took 15 votes to finally elect a Speaker of the House. I think you have more raw motions at this point, and quite frankly, I'm not sure why anybody would even want this speakership right now, and that the position really lacks the ability.",
