  {
    "episode_id": 71281,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71281.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "Look, I think that, you know, some interesting dynamic is anyone who they come out in support of I think is going to cause a lot of other Republicans to really have a distaste for. And so it's a very interesting dynamic that we're seeing right now. Look, there are a lot of good people who have thrown their name in the ring, but I've been very clear that we're not going to make a commitment right now. Obviously, you know, any speaker from Louisiana would be fantastic, but I want to be clear. We're not going to make any commitments right now at all. And here's why. I think one of the first things you've got to do is you've got to actually establish stability to the position. The fact that any one person can come out and can effectively cause this motion of vacate is totally inappropriate. Jake, you know this. This is third in line to President of the United States. We don't need to have the kind of chaos and instability that we saw yesterday.",
